                  %a{:href => "#classical_homotopy_theory"} Classical homotopy theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#SimplicialPresheaves"} Simplicial presheaves
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#MonoidalPresheaves"} Monoidal presheaves
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#homological_algebra_and_stable_homotopy_theory"} Homological algebra and stable homotopy theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#categorical_model_structures"} Categorical model structures
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#model_structure_on_objects"}
                    Model structure on
                    = succeed "-objects" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi G
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#model_structure_on_monoids"} Model structure on monoids
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em monoidal model category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            which is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            in a compatible way. In particular, its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            inherits a closed monoidal structure, as does the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            that it presents.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #MonoidalModelCategory.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A (symmetric)
              %strong monoidal model category
              is
            %ul
              %li
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              equipped with the further
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              of
            %ul
              %li
                a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ,
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, I)
            %p such that the following two compatibility conditions are satisfied:
            %ol
              %li#PushoutProductAxiom
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"}> pushout-product axiom
                  ) For every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi X
                          %mo ′
                          %mo →
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ′
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f' \colon X' \to Y'
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product"} pushout-product
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} cofibered
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  over ways of forming the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                  of these objects
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⨿
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi X
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ′
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (X \otimes Y')
                        \\overset
                        {X \otimes X'}
                        {\amalg}
                        (Y \otimes X')
                        \\longrightarrow
                        Y \otimes Y'
                        \\,,
                %p
                  is itself a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibration"} acyclic
                  (i.e. also a
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  or
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
                  is so.
                %p
                  (Equivalently this says that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi C
                        %mo ×
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes \colon C \times C \to C
                  is a left
                  = succeed ".)" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
              %li#UnitAxiom
                %p
                  (unit axiom) For every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  and every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Q
                        %mi I
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi I
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \hookrightarrow Q I \stackrel{p_I}{\longrightarrow} I
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                        %mi I
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi I
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi X
                        %mi I
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Q I \otimes X
                        \\stackrel{p_I \otimes X}{\longrightarrow}
                        I\otimes X \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} X
                %p
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            %p
          %p
          #InternalHomQuillenAdjunction.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (internal hom Quillen adjunction)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∅
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∃
                        %mo !
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varnothing \overset{\exists !}{\to} X
              a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
            %p
              In this case the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes (-)
              preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,-]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Quillen+functor"} left Quillen functor
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi Qu
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{[X,-]}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{X\otimes(-)}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\bot_{\mathrlap{Qu}}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    }
                    \\mathcal{C}
            %p
          %p
          #MeaningOfPushoutProductAxiom.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (meaning of the pushout product axiom)
              %br/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              (
              %a{:href => "#PushoutProductAxiom"}> above
              ) is stronger than its implied statement in Exp.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InternalHomQuillenAdjunction"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %p
              It is at this point that the established tradition to just say “monoidal model category” for the above definition is somewhat misleading, in that Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              is really a model-category theoretic version of the stronger concept of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+categories"} closed monoidal
              categories (
              %em symmetric
              closed monoidal really, but the symmetry is not the subtle part). The arguably more accurate terminology “closed monoidal model category” for Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              is probably being avoided because
              %a{:href => "#Quillen67"} Quillen (1967)
              originally introduced model categories in general under the name “closed model categories” with the adjective “closed”
              %em not
              meant to refer to its use in
              = succeed "\u2026" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+categories"} closed categories
            %p
              Namely, the full strength of the pushout-product axiom is needed to imply that not only the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
              but also its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-] \,\colon\, C^{op} \times C \to C
              is homotopically well-behaved, to wit that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
              satisfies the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback-power+axiom"} pullback-power axiom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,-]
              but also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,A]
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functors"} right Quillen functors
              for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+objects"} cofibrant objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              In short, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              is the model-category theoretic way to ensure that not just the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              as well as their joint relatin in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-variable+adjunction"} two-variable adjunction
              are homotopically meaningful.
          %p
          #CaseOfCofibrantTensorUnit.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (cofibrant tensor unit implies unit axiom)
              %br/
              As a special case of Rem.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InternalHomQuillenAdjunction"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              happens to be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+objects"} cofibrant
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              is already implied by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#PushoutProductAxiom"} pushout-product axiom
            %p
              (Because then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q I \to I
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+objects"} cofibrant objects
              and such are preserved by functors that preserve acyclic cofibrations, by
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ken+Brown%27s+lemma"} Ken Brown's lemma
          #MonoidAxiom.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+axiom"}> monoid axiom
                )
            %p
              One says that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+axiom"} monoid axiom
              if every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              that is obtained as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\otimes f
              of acyclic cofibrations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              with any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley00"}> Schwede-Shipley 00, def. 3.3.
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In particular, the axiom in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidAxiom"}
              says that for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes (-)
              sends acyclic cofibrations to weak equivalences.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#MonoidalHomotopyCategory Monoidal homotopy category
          %h4#abstractly Abstractly
          #LocalizationFunctorIsLaxMonoidal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C},\otimes)
              a monoidal model category, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes^L
              of the tensor product makes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category of the model category
