          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#classical_homotopy_theory Classical homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nice+category+of+spaces"} nice category of topological spaces
                with cartesian product and the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            %li
              %p
                The category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                with cartesian product and the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+pointed+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on pointed topological spaces
                or pointed simplicial sets with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
                of pointed objects.
          %h3#SimplicialPresheaves Simplicial presheaves
          %p
            If the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            with respect to the standard
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves#MonoidalStructure"} Closed monoidal structure
          %h3#MonoidalPresheaves Monoidal presheaves
          %p
            More generally, if a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+model+category"} symmetric monoidal model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func\big(\mathcal{S}^{op}, \mathcal{M}\big)
            with its object-wise
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+functors"} projective model structure on functors
            is itself a monoidal model category (see
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Yalin12"} Yalin 2012, Lem. 3.8
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#White17"} White 2017, Cor. 5.20
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#PavlovScholbach18"} Pavlov &amp; Scholbach 2018, inside proof of Prop. 7.9
          %h3#homological_algebra_and_stable_homotopy_theory Homological algebra and stable homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
                with the usual
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
                carries various monoidal model category structures, see
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
          %p
            With respect to a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+symmetric+spectra"} model structure on symmetric spectra
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+orthogonal+spectra"} model structure on orthogonal spectra
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+excisive+functors"} model structure for excisive functors
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley00"}> Schwede-Shipley 00
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#MMSS00"} MMSS 00, theorem 12.1 (iii) with prop. 12.3
          %p The standard example of a monoidal model category whose unit is not cofibrant is the category of EKMM S-modules.
          %h3#categorical_model_structures Categorical model structures
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                with cartesian product and the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folk+model+structure"} folk model structure
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray"} Gray
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-categories
                with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray+tensor+product"} Gray tensor product
                and the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lack+model+structure"} Lack model structure
          %h3#model_structure_on_objects
            Model structure on
            = succeed "-objects" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .un_def
            %h6#assumption Assumption
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              equipped with the structure of
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            %p such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the model structure is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated
              %li
                %p
                  the tensor unit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  is cofibrant.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Under these conditions there is for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+model+structure"} Borel model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}^{\mathbf{B}G}
              of objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              equipped with a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} action
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{E}^{\mathbf{B}G} \to \mathcal{E}
            %p preserves and reflects fibrations and weak equivalences.
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BergerMoerdijkResolution"} Berger &amp; Moerdijk (2006) 2.5
