                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Model+Categories+and+More+General+Abstract+Homotopy+Theory"} Model Categories and More General Abstract Homotopy Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/dhk.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p (Mentioned in passing in Remark 55.10, with no definition given, but the preceding section discusses the pushout product axiom.)
          %p
            The term “pushout smash product” is used for the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+products"} smash products
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+category"} pointed categories
            (such as of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+simplicial+sets"} pointed simplicial sets
            or
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
              = succeed "," do
                %em Symmetric spectra
              %strong 13
              (1998) 149-208 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9801077"}> arXiv:math/9801077
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0894-0347-99-00320-3"} doi:10.1090/S0894-0347-99-00320-3
          %p The general notion of monoidal model categories and their pushout-product axiom appears in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebras and modules in monoidal model categories
                %strong 80
                2 (2000) 491-511 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9801082"}> arXiv:math/9801082
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/S002461150001220X"} doi:10.1112/S002461150001220X
            %li#Hovey98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
                , Def. 1.1 in:
                %em Monoidal model categories
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9803002"}> arXiv:math/9803002v1
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Although the earliest mentions of terminology appear to be these sources indicated above, the notion itself is older. In particular,
            %a{:href => "#Hovey99"} Hovey (1999), p. 107
            credits the definition of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Limit+Functors+on+Model+Categories+and+Homotopical+Categories"} Dwyer, Hirschhorn, Kan Smith (2004)
            (which had for years earlier been “in preparation”), and the definition is of course just a small variant of the definition
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+categories"} enriched model categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+categories"} simplicial model categories
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Quillen67
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
              , chapter II, section 2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopical+Algebra"} Homotopical Algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 43
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0097438"} doi:10.1007/BFb0097438
          %p
            (The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback-power+axiom"} pullback-power axiom
            is axiom “SM7” in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#Quillen67"} Quillen (1967)
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+axiom"} unit axiom
            together with the fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            is monoidal in this case is due to Hovey.
          %p
            Conditions for the existence of induced monoidal model structure on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+categories"} Reedy model categories
          %ul
            %li#Barwick10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
              , p. 282 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em On left and right model categories and left and right Bousfield localizations
              %strong 12
              2 (2010) 245–320 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4310/hha.2010.v12.n2.a9"}> doi:10.4310/hha.2010.v12.n2.a9
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/homology-homotopy-and-applications/volume-12/issue-2/On-left-and-right-model-categories-and-left-and-right/hha/1296223884.full"} euclid:1296223884
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2067"} arXiv:0708.2067
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2832"} arXiv:0708.2832
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.3435"} arXiv:0708.3435
          %p Some relevant homotopy category background:
          %ul
            %li#Shulman11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Comparing composites of left and right derived functors
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0706.2868"} arXiv:0706.2868
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://nyjm.albany.edu/j/2011/17-5.html"} publisher
          %p
            The monoidal structures for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            are due to
          %ul
            %li#SchwedeShipley00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                %em Algebras and modules in monoidal model categories
                Proc. London Math. Soc. (2000) 80(2): 491-511 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uic.edu/~bshipley/monoidal.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#MMSS00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"} Stefan Schwede
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Model+categories+of+diagram+spectra"} Model categories of diagram spectra
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/mmssLMSDec30.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://plms.oxfordjournals.org/content/82/2/441.short?rss=1&ssource=mfc"} publisher
          %p Further variation of the axiomatics is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#BataninBerger13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Batanin"}> Michael Batanin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"} Clemens Berger
              %em Homotopy theory for algebras over polynomial monads
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1305.0086"}> arXiv:1305.0086
              )
          %p
            The monoidal model structure on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+model+structure"} Borel model structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}^{\mathbf{B}G}
            is discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#BergerMoerdijkResolution
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"}> Clemens Berger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Boardman-Vogt resolution of operads in monoidal model categories
              %strong 45
              (2006) 807-849 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0502155"}> arXiv:math/0502155
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.top.2006.05.001"} doi:10.1016/j.top.2006.05.001
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,1)-categories
            (in particular, that every locally presentable symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li#NikolausSagave15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steffen+Sagave"} Steffen Sagave
              %em Presentably symmetric monoidal infinity-categories are represented by symmetric monoidal model categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01475"}> arXiv:1506.01475
              )
          %p Monoidal Reedy model structures are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Moncef Ghazel, Fethi Kadhi,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Reedy diagrams in V-model categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.06535"} arXiv:1610.06535
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-019-09566-w"} doi:10.1007/s10485-019-09566-w
          %p
            On enhancement of monoidal model categories up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Quillen+adjunction"} monoidal
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          %ul
            %li#PavlovScholbach18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Pavlov"}> Dmitri Pavlov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jakob+Scholbach"} Jakob Scholbach
              = succeed "," do
                %em Admissibility and rectification of colored symmetric operads
              %strong 11
              3 (2018) 559-601 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/topo.12008"}> doi:10.1112/topo.12008
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.5675"} arXiv:1410.5675
          %p
            and for monoidal
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+categories"} simplicial model categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haldun+%C3%96zg%C3%BCr+Bay%C4%B1nd%C4%B1r"}> Haldun Özgür Bayındır
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Chorny"} Boris Chorny
              = succeed "," do
                %em Admissible replacements for simplicial monoidal model categories
              %strong 23
              (2023) 43-73 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.00515"}> arXiv:2008.00515
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2023.23.43"} doi:10.2140/agt.2023.23.43
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Yalin12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sinan+Yalin"}> Sinan Yalin
                , Lem 3.8 in version 1 of:
                %em Classifying spaces and moduli spaces of algebras over a prop
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.2964v1"}> arXiv:1207.2964v1
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#White17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+White"}> David White
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Model Structures on Commutative Monoids in General Model Categories
                %strong 221
                12 (2017) 3124-3168 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1403.6759"}> arXiv:1403.6759
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2017.03.001"} doi:10.1016/j.jpaa.2017.03.001
        .revisedby
